==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Midsummer Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves Into '''Brightsummer Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
At first glance, Midsummer Rabbit may appear to have similar issues to her original counterpart, in that she lacks the base stats to be useful in her Evolved Form, but her base stats for both attack and defense are 15% higher than her original counterpart. This, combined with her great range and many knockbacks that allow her to be pushed to safety easily, makes her a solid unit in general, although far from the best.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Adding onto her base stats, her first form has a 100% chance to slow [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies for 4.6 seconds (without [[Fruit Treasures]]), which is very good, primarily because her range is so high. However, her uptime on said ability is not enough to control them effectively all the time, as it is almost ten whole seconds before Midsummer Rabbit will attack again. This means she will not preserve your stack on her own, which is unfortunate and shows in stages like [[Gestalt, Decay]] and [[Rutsborg Vortex]].

It is, therefore, recommended to use her with tankers like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] or [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]], as they can take the brutality of the battle long enough for Rabbit to apply her debuffs again. With that being said, there are other Cats who can control those previously mentioned traits extremely well, those cats in mention being [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] for Dark enemies and talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] for Angels. Thus, only use this form in place of the Evolved Form if you want an extra layer of crowd control (provided you have those cats) or need the ranged support.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Everything previously said about this unit's good stats is simply amplified against her targets in this form, making Midsummer Cat a solid unit when it comes to damaging Black and Angel enemies from a distance. Although she can get overwhelmed in between two attacks, she can be expected to make full use of her knockbacks and only die after having left a noticeable mark.

==='''True Form'''===
Midsummer Rabbit's True Form, '''Brightsummer Cat''', is what happens if you combine the abilities of her previous two forms together while slapping [[Knockback|Knockback]] and [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]] on her. She is solid overall, with Wave Immunity further improving her performance in mixed stages, while keeping aggressive Black and Angel enemies away from most units in said mixed stages.

Overall, an excellent, long sought-after True Form with a cheap [[Catfruit]] cost.

